about what the circumcenter of the reflected triangle is.\n\nActually, let me just compute numerically first to get the answer, then verify.\n\nG_A = (19/3, -4) ≈ (6.3333, -4)\nG_B = (923/75, 212/25) = (12.3067, 8.48)\nG_C = (-821/507, 1236/169) ≈ (-1.6193, 7.3136)\n\nCircumcenter of these three points.\n\nLet me use the perpendicular bisector method.\n\nMidpoint of G_A G_B: ((6.3333+12.3067)/2, (-4+8.48)/2) = (9.32, 2.24)\nDirection G_A to G_B: (12.3067-6.3333, 8.48-(-4)) = (5.9733, 12.48)\nPerp bisector: 5.9733(x-9.32) + 12.48(y-2.24) = 0\n\nMidpoint of G_A G_C: ((6.3333-1.6193)/2, (-4+7.3136)/2) = (2.357, 1.6568)\nDirection G_A to G_C: (-1.6193-6.3333, 7.3136-(-4)) = (-7.9527, 11.3136)\nPerp bisector: -7.9527(x-2.357) + 11.3136(y-1.6568) = 0\n\nFrom equation 1: 5.9733 x - 55.672 + 12.48 y - 27.955 = 0 → 5.9733 x + 12.48 y = 83.627\nFrom equation 2: -7.9527 x + 18.745 + 11.3136 y - 18.745 = 0... let me recompute.\n-7.9527(x-2.357) + 11.3136(y-1.6568) = 0\n-7.9527 x + 18.745 + 11.3136 y - 18.745 = 0\nWait: 7.9527 × 2.357 = 18.745. 11.3136 × 1.6568 = 18.745. Interesting, they're equal!\nSo: -7.9527 x + 11.3136 y = 0 → y = 7.9527/11.3136 x = 0.7029 x\n\nFrom eq 1: 5.9733 x + 12.48(0.7029 x) = 83.627\n5.9733 x + 8.772 x = 83.627\n14.745 x = 83.627\nx = 5.6716\ny = 0.7029 × 5.6716 = 3.986\n\nSo O_G ≈ (5.6716, 3.986).\n\nHmm, interesting. Let me check: G = (19/3, 4) ≈ (6.333, 4). O_G ≈ (5.672, 3.986). Close to G but not the same.\n\nNow X is where line A-O_G meets BC (y=0).\nA = (5, 12), O_G ≈ (5.6716, 3.986).\nDirection: (5.6716-5, 3.986-12) = (0.6716, -8.014)\nParametric: (5 + 0.6716 t, 12 - 8.014 t). Set y=0: t = 12/8.014 = 1.4974.\nx = 5 + 0.6716 × 1.4974 = 5 + 1.0056 = 6.0056.\n\nSo X ≈ (6.006, 0). Y = (7, 0).\nXY = |7 - 6.006| = 0.994 ≈ 1?\n\nHmm, that's close to 1. Let me be more precise.\n\nActually let me redo this with exact arithmetic. This is important.\n\nLet me use exact fractions.\n\nG_A = (19/3, -4)\nG_B = (923/75, 212/25)\nG_C = (-821/507, 1236/169)\n\n