umerical estimate. ✓\n\nNow, X is where line from A=(5,12) to O_G=(1673/295, 1176/295) meets y=0.\n\nDirection: O_G - A = (1673/295 - 5, 1176/295 - 12) = (1673/295 - 1475/295, 1176/295 - 3540/295) = (198/295, -2364/295).\n\nParametric: P(t) = A + t·(O_G - A) = (5 + 198t/295, 12 - 2364t/295).\nSet y = 0: 12 - 2364t/295 = 0 → t = 12·295/2364 = 3540/2364.\nSimplify: 3540/2364. Divide by 12: 295/197. \nCheck: 3540/12 = 295, 2364/12 = 197. 197 is prime. 295 = 5·59. gcd=1. So t = 295/197.\n\nx = 5 + 198·(295/197)/295 = 5 + 198/197 = (985 + 198)/197 = 1183/197.\n\nSo X = (1183/197, 0).\n\nY = (7, 0) = (1379/197, 0).\n\nXY = |1379/197 - 1183/197| = 196/197.\n\nSo XY = 196/197. a = 196, b = 197. a + b = 393.\n\nWait, let me double-check that 196/197 is irreducible. gcd(196, 197). 197 is prime. 196 = 4·49 = 2²·7². 197 is prime and doesn't divide 196. So yes, irreducible.\n\na + b = 196 + 197 = 393.\n\nLet me verify the key steps once more.\n\nThe reflection computations:\n- G_A: reflect G=(19/3,4) across BC (y=0): (19/3, -4). ✓\n- G_B: reflect G across AC (4x+3y-56=0): got (923/75, 212/25). ✓\n- G_C: reflect G across AB (12x-5y=0): got (-821/507, 1236/169). ✓\n\nThe circumcenter:\n- From |O-G_A|²=|O-G_C|², we got -1344u + 1912v = 0, so v = 168u/239.\n- From |O-G_A|²=|O-G_B|², we got 56u + 117v = 784.\n- Substituting: 56u + 117·168u/239 = 784 → u(56 + 19656/239) = 784 → u(13384+19656)/239 = 784 → u·33040/239 = 784 → u = 784·239/33040.\n  784·239 = 187376. 187376/33040. Let me simplify: gcd(187376, 33040).\n  33040 = 16·2065 = 16·5·7·59. \n  187376/16 = 11711. So 187376/33040 = 11711/2065 = 1673/295. ✓\n- v = 168·1673/(239·295) = 281064/70505. 281064/239 = 1176. So v = 1176/295. ✓\n\nLine A to O_G:\n- A=(5,12) = (1475/295, 3540/295), O_G=(1673/295, 1176/295).\n- Direction: (198/295, -2364/295) = (198, -2364)/295.\n- At y=0: t = 12·295/2364 = 3540/2364 = 295/197.\n- x = 5 + (198/295)·(295/197) = 5 + 198/197 = (985+198)/197 = 1183/197. ✓\n\nXY = 7 - 1183/197 = (1379-1183)/197 = 196/197. ✓\n\na+b = 393.\n\nLet me also verify the circumcenter is correct by checking distances.\n\n|O_G - G_A|² = (1673/295 - 19/3)² + (1176/295 + 4)²\n= (1673/295 - 19·295/(3·295))²... wait, 19/3 = 19·295/(3·295)? No, let me use common denominator.\n1673/295 - 19/3 = (1673·3 - 19·295)/(295·3) = (5019 - 5605)/885 = -586/885.\n1176/295 + 4 = (1176 + 1180)/295 = 2356/295.\n\n|O_G - G_A|² = (586/885)² + (2356/295)² = 586²/885² + 2356²/295².\n= 343396/783225 + 5550736/87025.\n87025 = 295². 783225 = 885² = (3·295)² = 9·87025.\n5550736/87025 = 49956624/783225.\nSum = (343396 + 49956624)/783225 = 50300020/783225.\n\n|O_G - G_B|²: G_B = (923/75, 212/25).\n1673/295 - 923/75 = (1673·75 - 923·295)/(295·75) = (125475 - 272285)/22125 = -146810/22125.\nSimplify: 146810/22125. Divide by 5: 29362/4425. \n1176/295 - 212/25 = (1176·25 - 212·295)/(295·25) = (29400 - 62540)/7375 = -33140/7375.\nSimplify: 33140/7375. Divide by 5: 6628/1475.\n\nThis is getting complicated. Let me just trust the algebra since the two linear equations were derived correctly and the numerical check matched.\n\nActually, let me just verify numerically.\nO_G = (1673/295, 1176/295) ≈ (5.67119, 3.98644)\nG_A = (6.33333, -4)\n|O_G - G_A|² = (5.67119-6.33333)² + (3.98644+4)² = (-0.66214)² + (7.98644)² = 0.43843 + 63.7821 = 64.2206\n\nG_B = (12.30667, 8.48)\n|O_G - G_B|² = (5.67119-12.30667)² + (3.98644-8.48)² = (-6.63548)² + (-4.49356)² = 44.0296 + 20.1921 = 64.2217\n\nG_C = (-1.61933, 7.31361)\n|O_G - G_C|² = (5.67119+1.61933)² + (3.98644-7.31361)² = (7.29052)² + (-3.32717)² = 53.1517 + 11.0700 = 64.2217\n\nAll approximately equal (small rounding errors). ✓\n\nSo the answer is a + b = 196 + 197 = 393.\n\nLet me also double check Y. The centroid G lies on the median from A to the midpoint of BC. Midpoint of BC = ((0+14)/2, (0+0)/2) = (7, 0). So Y = (7, 0). ✓\n\nAnd X = (1183/197, 0) ≈ (6.005, 0). XY = 7 - 6.005 = 0.995 ≈ 196/197 ≈ 0.9949. ✓\n\nThe answer is 393.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786708427}
